  "solution": "def find_missing_number(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    n = len(nums)\n    expected_sum = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    return expected_sum - sum(nums)\n",
  "explanation": "Sum of first N integers is N*(N+1)//2. Subtracting the array sum identifies the missing number in O(N) time and O(1) space."
